<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila posts $3.895 bln BOP surplus in yr to Nov27.</title>
<headline>Manila posts $3.895 bln BOP surplus in yr to Nov27.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines posted a balance of payments surplus of $3.895 billion in the year to November 27, up from a $259 million deficit registered in the same period last year, a Central Bank official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Central Bank director for research Diwa Gunigundo said the high surplus was due to the sustained influx of foreign investments into the country.</p>
